  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1218 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nLatest model data continues to support dry weather with temperatures\nwarming back to above seasonal levels through early next week, as \nupper level ridging builds back across the Great Basin and into \nthe Rockies. With weak flow aloft and at the surface limiting mixing, \nlatest NBM data is a tad lower with highs on Sunday than other guidance \nmay suggest. However, with ample sunshine and light winds, temperatures \nslightly above seasonal levels in the low 60s will likely feel warmer \nthan the ambient temperature indicates. \n\nThe upper ridge starts to flatten across the Rockies on Monday, with \nslightly more downslope flow leading to better mixing and warmer temperatures \nin the mid to upper 60s across the plains both Monday and Tuesday, and \nmainly in the 50s to lower 60s across the higher terrain. A passing wave \nacross the Northern Rockies Tuesday night looks to send a dry front across \nthe plains and leading to slightly cooler, but still around seasonal \ntemperatures on Wednesday. Upper level ridging then looks to rebuild across\nthe Central Rockies through the end of the work week, leading to continued\ndry conditions along with at and above seasonal temperatures.",
